                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Positiv:\n\n+ The latest update added a lot of menu options: 3 Difficulty settings, Sound/locomotion options. Very fast fix thanks!\n+ No longer nauseating they added teleport locomotion!\n+ The game is fun\n+ Good graphics\n+ Good menu (big fonts, clear easy to navigate)\n+ Very good sounds\n+ Good atmosphere (spectators!)\n+ Highscores\n+ Feels well polished overall with some things left coud easy be fixed\n+ The minigames are brilliant and funny (can we have more?)\n+ Slow motion effetcs\n+ Very exact implementation of original rules\n\nNeutral:\n\n° \"Funny\" game modes allow infinite shuttlecock shoots out of that mashine and they all fly in exactly the same path. The result is that you just need to swing the arm in the air left and right and cheat your way through the waves untill you feel tired of doing it that way. Need to fix it by making the path slightly random!\n° missing a \"free play\" mode where the enemy always plays back no matter where you hit or how bad your serve was (EDIT: They added amateur difficulty that comes realy close to a free play mode)\n* Missing different graphics options\n* They fixed the serve, the vive controller is no longer hiding the shuttlecock and it only falls when you let the trigger go. But I woud still prefere an option to hide the controller\n\nNegative:\n- The scale of everything is a bit too small the racket feels small compared to a vive controller the playspace feels smaller then the offical 13,4m x 6,1m\n- There is no reason to move the player while doing a serve please fix this\n- Noticed a bug where you can smash the shuttlecock through the net sometimes and get a positiv score for it.",
